    "result_text": "I added the `ratelimit` decorator and applied it to the team-creation form. I couldn't run the tests because the test command needs approval, which wasn't granted in this session.\n\n- **Decorator:** `ratelimit(method=\"POST\", limit=50, interval=300, key_prefix=\"rl\")` is now in `CTFd/utils/decorators/__init__.py`. It uses the catalog pattern `decorators.ratelimit@v1`, and the `# pcat:` marker is kept. It counts requests per client IP and endpoint in the cache. Once the limit is hit, it returns a JSON 429. `check_code` reported no deviations from the pattern.\n- **Missing definition:** `auth.py`, `teams.py`, `events` and several API modules already import and use `ratelimit` from that module, but it wasn't defined there. This commit adds it, so those imports should resolve again.\n- **Login, register and team join:** these were already decorated, so I left them alone.\n  - `login` and `register` in `CTFd/auth.py` use `@ratelimit(method=\"POST\", limit=10, interval=5)`.\n  - `/teams/join` in `CTFd/teams.py` uses the same limits.\n- **Team creation:** `/teams/new` was the one team form without a limit. I added `@ratelimit(method=\"POST\", limit=10, interval=5)` to it.\n- **Not covered:** `/teams/invite` also accepts POST and is not rate limited. Say if you want it covered too.\n\nTo run the checks yourself, use `pytest tests/utils/test_ratelimit.py tests/teams/test_auth.py`."
